@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "okta.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki To Okta Customer Group Integration
	Testing to assure koroneiki customer and group integration to okta works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
    * I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | okt.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OKT                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| OKTKOROKTKOR |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OKTKOROKTKOR |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Sync customer group membership via koroneiki to okta
	Koroneiki customer contacts with the proper group synced via Koroneiki should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | OKTKOROKTKOR                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTKOROKTKOR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync customer user email updates to okta
	Koroneiki customer contacts with subsequent email updates made via Koroneiki and synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | OKTKOROKTKOR                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTKOROKTKOR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address | okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.koroneiki2"
	And I click on the user with the name "OKT Koroneiki1" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	# Necessary pause for okta to sync correctly
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on okta
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync customer user name updates to okta
	Koroneiki customer contacts with subsequent name updates made via Koroneiki and synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | OKTKOROKTKOR                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTKOROKTKOR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| First Name | TKO        |
	| Last Name  | Koroneiki2 |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.koroneiki1"
	And I click on the user with the name "TKO Koroneiki2" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following user values in the user details page
	| Name               | TKO Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address      | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                             |
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	Then I should be able to view the following user values in the user details page
	| Name               | OKT Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address      | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                             |
	# Necessary pause for okta to sync correctly
	And I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on okta
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync customer user verification to okta
	Koroneiki customer contacts with subsequent verification updates made via Koroneiki and synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | OKTKOROKTKOR                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTKOROKTKOR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| Email Address Verified | false |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.koroneiki1"
	And I click on the user with the name "OKT Koroneiki1" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following user values in the user details page
	| Name               | OKT Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address      | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | UNVERIFIED                           |
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	Then I should be able to view the following user values in the user details page
	| Name               | OKT Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address      | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                    |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                             |
	# Necessary pause for okta to sync correctly
	When I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on okta
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

Scenario: Sync customer user uuid to okta
	Koroneiki customer contacts with subsequent uuid updates made via Koroneiki and synced via Provisioning should be properly synced to okta.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | OKTKOROKTKOR                         | |
	| Contact Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test okt account on koroneiki        | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                  | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}        | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Profile Email Address | okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                        | |
	| Status                | Active                               | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                   | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikicorporation.com         | |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | true                     | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles	
	| Support User |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	Then the support organization with the code "OKTKOROKTKOR" should be part of the support site
	And the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be a member of the okta group "Customers"
	When I update a koroneiki contact with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to have the following values
	| UUID | 1234abcd-56ef-78gh-90ij-123456klmnop |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "okt.koroneiki1"
	And I click on the user with the name "OKT Koroneiki1" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the sync with okta button in the user details page
	Then I should be able to view the contact account with the name "Oktkor - ${staticProjectName}" and the following values
	| Name          | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code          | OKTKOROKTKOR                  |
	| Region        | United States                 |
	| Roles         | Support User                  |
	| Teams         | Oktkor - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Account State | ACTIVE                        |
	# Necessary pause for okta to sync correctly
	When I wait for "10" seconds
	Then the user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be present on okta
	And the koroneiki contact and the okta user with the email address "okt.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should have matching uuid values

